                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "An exhibition at the museum of PC DOS games.  I played Rogue and then Hack on my first PC back in mid 80's.  Yeah, the early days of game design was brutal.  No balance, no predictable progression, just pure luck.  You died.  A lot.  Might and Magic, Wizardry.  All of them should be titled 'You're Dead'.  \r\n\r\nFast forward half a century.  Game design has evolved, so this game is best sampled as nostalgia *malicious chuckle*, or for the younger generation, something to respect what pain older generation endured for gaming entertainment.  Sample it, don't lose your sanity.",
